<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt936" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwEto" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite book\n ","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Adams"},"first":{"wt":"S."},"year":{"wt":"1997"},"title":{"wt":"Relativity: An Introduction to Space–Time Physics"},"url":{"wt":"https://books.google.com/books?id=1RV0AysEN4oC&amp;pg=PA140"},"page":{"wt":"140"},"publisher":{"wt":"CRC Press"},"isbn":{"wt":"978-0-7484-0621-0"},"quote":{"wt":"One peculiar consequence of this system of definitions is that any future refinement in our ability to measure&amp;nbsp;{{mvar|c}} will not change the speed of light (which is a defined number), but will change the length of the meter!"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFAdams1997" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt936">Adams, S. (1997). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://books.google.com/books?id=1RV0AysEN4oC&amp;pg=PA140" class="external text" id="mwEts"><i id="mwEtw">Relativity: An Introduction to Space–Time Physics</i></a>. CRC Press. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwEt0"> </span>140. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEt4">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwEt8"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-7484-0621-0" title="Special:BookSources/978-0-7484-0621-0" id="mwEuA"><bdi id="mwEuE">978-0-7484-0621-0</bdi></a>. <q id="mwEuI">One peculiar consequence of this system of definitions is that any future refinement in our ability to measure<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwEuM"> </span><span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" id="mwEuQ">c</span> will not change the speed of light (which is a defined number), but will change the length of the meter!</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=Relativity%3A+An+Introduction+to+Space%E2%80%93Time+Physics&amp;rft.pages=140&amp;rft.pub=CRC+Press&amp;rft.date=1997&amp;rft.isbn=978-0-7484-0621-0&amp;rft.aulast=Adams&amp;rft.aufirst=S.&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fbooks.google.com%2Fbooks%3Fid%3D1RV0AysEN4oC%26pg%3DPA140&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASpeed+of+light" class="Z3988" about="#mwt936" id="mwEuU"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-W_Rindler-177" id="cite_note-W_Rindler-177" data-mw-footnote-number="175"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEuY"><a href="#cite_ref-W_Rindler_177-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEuc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEug">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-W_Rindler-177" class="mw-reference-text reference-text">
<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt939" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwEuk" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite book\n ","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Rindler"},"first":{"wt":"W."},"author-link":{"wt":"Wolfgang Rindler"},"year":{"wt":"2006"},"title":{"wt":"Relativity: Special, General, and Cosmological"},"url":{"wt":"https://books.google.com/books?id=MuuaG5HXOGEC&amp;pg=PT41"},"page":{"wt":"41"},"edition":{"wt":"2"},"publisher":{"wt":"Oxford University Press"},"isbn":{"wt":"978-0-19-856731-8"},"quote":{"wt":"Note that [...] improvements in experimental accuracy will modify the meter relative to atomic wavelengths, but not the value of the speed of light!"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFRindler2006" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt939"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolfgang_Rindler" title="Wolfgang Rindler" id="mwEuo">Rindler, W.</a> (2006). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://books.google.com/books?id=MuuaG5HXOGEC&amp;pg=PT41" class="external text" id="mwEus"><i id="mwEuw">Relativity: Special, General, and Cosmological</i></a> (2<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwEu0"> </span>ed.). Oxford University Press. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwEu4"> </span>41. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEu8">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwEvA"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-19-856731-8" title="Special:BookSources/978-0-19-856731-8" id="mwEvE"><bdi id="mwEvI">978-0-19-856731-8</bdi></a>. <q id="mwEvM">Note that [...] improvements in experimental accuracy will modify the meter relative to atomic wavelengths, but not the value of the speed of light!</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=Relativity%3A+Special%2C+General%2C+and+Cosmological&amp;rft.pages=41&amp;rft.edition=2&amp;rft.pub=Oxford+University+Press&amp;rft.date=2006&amp;rft.isbn=978-0-19-856731-8&amp;rft.aulast=Rindler&amp;rft.aufirst=W.&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fbooks.google.com%2Fbooks%3Fid%3DMuuaG5HXOGEC%26pg%3DPT41&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASpeed+of+light" class="Z3988" about="#mwt939" id="mwEvQ"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-178" id="cite_note-178" data-mw-footnote-number="176"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEvU"><a href="#cite_ref-178" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEvY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEvc">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-178" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt944" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwEvg" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"url":{"wt":"http://www.bipm.org/en/si/new_si/explicit_constant.html"},"title":{"wt":"The \"explicit-constant\" formulation"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20140811195806/http://www.bipm.org/en/si/new_si/explicit_constant.html"},"archive-date":{"wt":"11 August 2014"},"website":{"wt":"BIPM"},"date":{"wt":"2011"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt944" id="mwEvk"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20140811195806/http://www.bipm.org/en/si/new_si/explicit_constant.html" class="external text" id="mwEvo">"The "explicit-constant" formulation"</a>. <i id="mwEvs">BIPM</i>. 2011. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.bipm.org/en/si/new_si/explicit_constant.html" class="external text" id="mwEvw">the original</a> on 11 August 2014.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=BIPM&amp;rft.atitle=The+%22explicit-constant%22+formulation&amp;rft.date=2011&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.bipm.org%2Fen%2Fsi%2Fnew_si%2Fexplicit_constant.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASpeed+of+light" class="Z3988" about="#mwt944" id="mwEv0"></span></span></li>
